(3696,3696,1,'Web-Based Artificial Intelligence Model for Predicting Complications After CT-Guided Transthoracic Lung Tumor Biopsy','<p>Computed tomography-guided transthoracic lung biopsy is an important minimally invasive technique for obtaining tissue from peripheral pulmonary lesions. However, pneumothorax and pulmonary parenchymal hemorrhage remain frequent complications, and accurately estimating an individual patient’s risk before and during the procedure remains challenging. This study aimed to develop a web-based artificial intelligence-enabled prediction model for estimating the risks of pneumothorax and pulmonary parenchymal hemorrhage after computed tomography-guided transthoracic lung biopsy. A retrospective dataset of 141 patients who underwent the procedure at Binh Dan Hospital between June 2019 and June 2023 was analyzed. Multivariable logistic regression models incorporating lesion size, lesion depth from the pleural surface, and number of needle passes were developed and implemented in a web-based clinical decision-support tool to provide individualized complication-risk estimates. The mean patient age was 63.87 years, 70.9% were male, and 65.2% had a history of smoking. Pneumothorax occurred in 29.7% of patients, with chest drainage required in 2.1%, while pulmonary parenchymal hemorrhage occurred in 46.1% and hemoptysis in 7.8%. The prediction models achieved accuracies of 79.4% for pneumothorax and 85.1% for pulmonary parenchymal hemorrhage. Smaller lesions, greater lesion depth, and a higher number of needle passes were associated with increased complication risk. The developed web-based model converts readily available anatomical and procedural variables into immediate individualized risk estimates. It may support patient counseling, procedural planning, optimization of needle sampling, and postbiopsy monitoring; however, external and prospective validation is required before routine clinical implementation.</p>','["Artificial intelligence", "Clinical decision support", "Computed tomography-guided transthoracic lung biopsy", "Pneumothorax", "Prediction model", "Pulmonary parenchymal hemorrhage"]',NULL,29,1,'2575 - 2584',NULL,'The Authors',2026,'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/','published','2026-09-17',3),
